think Lap N is 3994 by git rev-list, so the rota row is 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in. Read its threshold and all three seats. The previous lap in this tree read row 2 by hand and the modulus skipped row 3, Water, which I record rather than correct, since the seed sanctions advancing past a repeat and says nothing about a jump. Earth's instruction shaped the whole lap: take the concrete fact in at the door, and trust that first reading over the plausible story.
think Its Dual seat is the-marked-value -- every value crossing a seam wears a mark naming its type. That pointed straight at my own lane, because comlink/topology.rye's Address carries a tier and the tier is exactly such a mark. The card's own live front said DIFFUSER had measured the routing metric over 682,425 ordered pairs and found the metric reads that mark, so a distance depends on which outfit each end wears rather than on the two points alone.
think Opened the cold roster and held still for it. 116 rostered, 111 green, 1 red, 4 gated, tree_moved=no. The one red is agent_jail, and I checked it at a bare prompt rather than believing the card: bwrap --dev-bind / / true answers "Failed to make / slave: Operation not permitted" and unshare --user true answers "unshare failed: Operation not permitted", so this host denies the process a namespace. That is an environment fact, it is BAKERY's lane, and a peer has since booked it as %446. shell_dialect is green, which closes the sed -i pair the card named as mine -- a peer landed temp-then-cat at both sites.
think Read route_hops and its doc line: "Zero exactly when a and b are one point." Worked the arithmetic by hand first. Under the inclusive breach of_galaxy(8), of_star(8,0) and of_planet(8,0,0) all encode to 8, so they are one point; route_hops reads tier through depth(), so it answers 1 and 2 between them. That contradicts the line above the function.
think Refused to book it on arithmetic. Planted the doc's own sentence into the selftest as two assertions and built it. PlantNotOnePoint did not fire, which proved the two addresses really are one point; DocClaimRefused fired, which proved the function disagrees with the sentence above it. The module refused its own doc line on metal, and that is the red.
think Repaired the sentence to what the function keeps -- zero exactly when a and b are the same address, indices and outfit alike -- with a say-why naming both halves, matching the shape %439's repair used thirty lines up in the same file on the same day.
think Then pinned it, because a corrected sentence with no assert behind it drifts again. Three legs compare two outfits of ONE point, which no existing leg did: every one of the five named routing legs compares addresses at the same tier, so the degree of freedom inclusion opened had never been exercised.
think Built the half that holds as a real proof rather than a sentence. prove_route_is_never_blind walks every ordered pair of both seated skies -- 518,400 for the compass sky, 164,025 for the council -- asserting no two distinct points read zero hops apart. That is the one property routing cannot survive losing, the census had measured it true, and it had no guard.
obs THE PLANT THAT TAUGHT ME MOST WAS THE ONE THAT ALMOST DIDN'T RED. My first attempt to prove the new proof can refuse made route_hops return 0 for every same-galaxy pair, and the existing leg PlanetToStarNotOne caught it before my proof ever ran -- which proves nothing about my proof. So I planted an alias in galaxy 11, a corner no named leg visits, and got RouteBlindBetweenPoints while all eight named legs passed. That is the reading worth keeping: the pairwise walk sees a fault that eight hand-picked pairs cannot, and I only know it because the first plant failed to isolate.
obs THE CLASS IS %439's, ONE STEP HARDER. That row was a number in a comment disagreeing with a constant thirty lines above -- a reader can hold 792 against 720. This is the word "point", which inclusion redefined when an address and a point stopped being one-to-one, and no grep reaches a definition. The last lap measured the number class tree-wide and found one true positive in 159; this half of the class has no detector at all, and I am not proposing one, because a meter that reads what a word means is a meter I cannot build honestly today.
obs I TOOK TWO OF ANOTHER SHIP'S NAMED BUILDABLES AND SAY SO PLAINLY. DIFFUSER's essay named three things for BAKERY: seat_arc, a zero-hop witness, and one doc line on route_hops. Two of those are this lap. The roster draws lanes by territory and comlink/ is this seat's, so this is my own lane's work that a peer suggested elsewhere rather than a claim-as-override -- yet the risk of duplicate effort is real, so it is named here, on the day shelf, and on the card. seat_arc stays proposed: adding a public function is a design act and the essay calls it a proposal itself.
obs THE ESSAY PROPOSED AN ADDITION WHERE A CORRECTION WAS OWED. Its third item asks for a doc line "naming that its answer depends on the tier each address carries." That is true and it is not the whole fact: the standing sentence was not thin, it was false, and adding a line beside it would have left both standing. Reading the file at the door rather than reading the proposal about the file is the only reason I saw it -- which is Earth's instruction working exactly as written.
obs THE CARD PAID FOR THE ROOM BEFORE IT SPENT IT. It stood 105 bytes from its 32,768 ceiling, so the DIFFUSER census block -- 2,509 bytes, closed on every count, with two of its three buildables now built and its agent_jail fact booked upstream -- folded whole to construction/archive/20260906-005436_itinerary-landed-accounts.md behind a cairn at nib 41998f8835. A fold rather than a raise, because the living parts had not grown; what had grown was a closed account whose findings now live in a witness.
obs THE SPINE MADE ME ADOPT BEFORE I COULD BOOK. reds_spine_derive_scan --next read 447 after the fetch, and the monotone witness refused it, because 446 was upstream and not yet in this tree -- 1..N with a hole. Adopting xy first and re-reading gave the same 447 on a whole spine. Two headline numbers move with a row and only one is derived: the remainder 426 -> 427 and the span "1 to 446" -> "1 to 447", the second of which no arithmetic catches and the headline scan does.
